ENGLISH — GOVERNING TEXT

1. Scope and definitions

This license applies to the WebFence source code, executables and documentation
expressly offered under it (the "Software"). "Author" means Matteo Luigi
Feroldi. Third-party components, datasets and model weights remain subject to
their own licenses and are not relicensed by this document.

An "Individual" is a natural person acting on their own account. An
"Independent Professional" is an Individual personally performing professional
services for clients, including as a self-employed practitioner or sole
professional proprietor. This does not include a company, an incorporated
practice, or a person using the Software in their capacity as an employee,
officer or internal operator of a Company.

A "Company" is an incorporated business, commercial partnership or other
organization operating a business, including a business sole proprietorship
other than the Independent Professional described above. Merely employing a
person does not prevent that person's unrelated personal use from qualifying.

2. Free grant

Subject to these terms, each copyright holder offering their work under this
license grants Individuals a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright
license to access, download, run, reproduce, study, modify and create forks or
derivative works of the Software for:

(a) personal noncommercial use, learning, experimentation and research; and
(b) use by an Independent Professional to perform professional assessments,
    including paid assignments for clients that are Companies.

An Independent Professional may operate their own copy on equipment they
control, including rented infrastructure. This permission does not permit a
client Company to install, operate, control or access the Software itself.
Assessing a Company's target and delivering the resulting report do not, by
themselves, constitute Company use of the Software.

3. Free redistribution and forks

Individuals may share original or modified source code and executables without
charge with other Individuals for the purposes in section 2. Distributions
must include this license and existing copyright and attribution notices,
identify modifications, and not claim that a modified version is an official
release. Recipients obtain rights to the original work under this license;
redistributors may not remove its restrictions or grant broader rights to it.
Contributions distributed as part of a modified version must be offered under
these terms to the extent the distributor has the necessary rights.

Public source-code hosting, viewing and repository forks through GitHub or a
comparable source hosting service are permitted, including incidental copies
needed to provide that service. A public repository does not authorize Company
operation of the Software or commercial redistribution. Rights independently
granted by a hosting platform's applicable terms are not withdrawn here.

4. Uses requiring separate written authorization

Prior written authorization from Matteo Luigi Feroldi is required for:

(a) installation or use of the Software by a Company, including internal use,
    use by its employees or contractors as its internal operators, and use of
    a modified version;
(b) distribution, licensing or provision of the Software to a Company for its
    use, even without charge;
(c) selling, renting, sublicensing for a fee or otherwise commercially
    distributing the Software or derivatives containing it; and
(d) offering third parties hosted, managed, automated or API access to the
    Software, including scanner-as-a-service offerings.

Charging for an Independent Professional's own assessment and delivering its
results under section 2(b) is expressly allowed and is not prohibited by (c)
or (d). Giving a client access to operate the scanner is a separate use.
Any other use outside the grants above requires separate permission from the
relevant rights holders.

5. Commercial agreements and royalties

The Author may grant separate written licenses for rights the Author controls.
Such agreements may be free or may specify fees, royalties, scope, duration,
support and redistribution rights. No royalty rate, payment obligation or
commercial authorization arises merely from this public license or from
submitting a request. Payment alone does not establish a license without an
agreement. A separate agreement overrides these terms only to the extent it
expressly provides and the granting party controls the relevant rights.

6. Reports and user data

This license does not claim ownership of targets, user data, findings or
reports generated through permitted use. To the extent a generated report
contains copyrightable WebFence report-template material, permission is
granted to reproduce, modify and deliver that material as part of the report,
including commercially. This exception does not cover Software executables
or source code included outside normal report-template content. Third-party
rights in evidence and data remain unaffected.

7. Authorized assessment

Use the Software only against targets you own or are authorized to assess,
within the permitted scope. This license grants no access rights to third-party
systems and does not replace the target owner's authorization.

8. Attribution, trademarks and contributions

Preserve copyright and license notices. No trademark rights or endorsement by
the Author are granted beyond factual attribution. Contributors retain their
copyrights. This license alone does not transfer their ownership or give the
Author the right to relicense their contributions commercially. Any additional
contribution agreement must be accepted separately and explicitly.

9. No warranty

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED
"AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
NON-INFRINGEMENT. NO SCAN, AI OUTPUT OR SIGNED REPORT GUARANTEES SECURITY,
COMPLETENESS OR THE ABSENCE OF VULNERABILITIES.

10. Limitation of liability

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE AUTHOR AND CONTRIBUTORS
ARE NOT LIABLE FOR CLAIMS, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE
OR ITS USE, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE. NOTHING IN THIS LICENSE
EXCLUDES LIABILITY OR RIGHTS THAT CANNOT LAWFULLY BE EXCLUDED.

11. Termination and existing rights

The grants apply while you comply with these terms. A material breach ends
your grants. On the first breach, the grants are reinstated if you stop the
violation and remedy it within 30 days after written notice from the relevant
rights holder. Later reinstatement requires that holder's written consent.
Compliant recipients retain their own grants. The Author's later release of
different license terms does not revoke compliant grants for copies already
received under this version.

12. Interpretation

Rights and exceptions that cannot be restricted under applicable law remain
unaffected. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue
